message: If you use this software, please cite it.
title: "Promises to whom: identifying personal guilt and partner-specific commitment across populations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hernández Gallegos
    given-names: Montserrat Ximena
repository-code: https://github.com/Montse2308/Dilema-del-Prisionero
url: https://github.com/Montse2308/Dilema-del-Prisionero
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-23
keywords:
  - evolutionary game theory
  - promises
  - guilt
  - commitment
abstract: >-
  Finite-population simulation of personal guilt and partner-specific
  commitment. Holding fixed the probability that the decider promises, the
  communication protocol does not select who survives. With the belief
  that a promise will be kept held at 0.76, the mean second-order belief
  of deciders without a partner switch in Vanberg (2008, Table I), the
  first mover observing the type, the outside-option cap off, and theta
  above 0.277, the material payoff to personal guilt is low at both ends
  of the population prior and high in the middle. The payoff to
  partner-specific commitment does not move.
